# `!echo hi` (bang: runs directly in the user's shell, never reaches the
# model) — internal/tui/inputmodes.go ClassifyInput, RunBang. Does not
# consume a faux turn.
#
# kiln has no `#` memory-note mode (dropped to match Claude Code, whose own
# prompt input has none - only a bash prefix and a plain prompt): a
# line starting with `#` is now an ordinary prompt, which this scenario
# confirms by sending one and seeing it echoed and answered like any other
# message, never "Saved to ... CLAUDE.md".
@faux testdata/faux/hello.yaml
@size 120x40

WAITFOR /describe a task/ 20
TYPE !echo hi
KEY enter
WAITFOR /shell ─/ 20
SHOT bang-echo
EXPECT /shell ─+\s+→ hi/
EXPECT_NOT /! echo hi/
EXPECT_NOT /Hello from faux/
TYPE #remember to run tests
KEY enter
WAITFOR /Hello from faux/ 20
SHOT hash-is-a-prompt
EXPECT /#remember to run tests/
EXPECT /Hello from faux/
EXPECT_NOT /Saved to/
EXPECT_NOT /panic|goroutine/
